  ("In a 32-bar MIDI clip, place a minimal chord shape and only a few slow sustained notes; then lower the pad cutoff slightly and let the reverb open it.","Piano roll","A slow, uncluttered harmonic bed."),
  ("Bass pad: new instance, saw through a 24 dB/oct low-pass, faster envelope with some decay, add a sine (or sine sub) layer and a touch of reverb; write one long root note.","Second synth","A solid low foundation that remains when the pad fades."),
  ("Detail voice: attack-decay envelope with sustain at zero, 24 dB low-pass with cutoff stepped by a slow sample-and-hold/step modulator; send heavily to delay and reverb; write a few sparse notes.","Third synth","Short rising-falling events whose brightness changes each hit, smeared into the space."),
